Z||000014||Topknot||05-25-2001||11:56 PM||||Sorry all for the delayed reaction and pictures...I have a set formatted...it's just that I went to the doc after trying to go back to work and found out I busted the dang thing in two places...Gotta watch those Fiero Blood Lusts!<P>Will post a web link in the next few days...so far it's proceeding nicely...I was able to remove all the strut..cambers..and "pop" off the joints without any major problems...also..I seem to be one of the lucky ones in that my axel came right out without nothing more than a slight crowbar pressure...surprised me after reading peep's postings of how "hard" there's was implanted...<P>The next steps is the hanging of the motor from above..with "special tool" 2x4 and chain..then gonna go for the half frame drop and hopefully tranny out this weekend..<P>Topknot =]<P>I will post just a couple of "r-13" pics of the mangled digits for others fare warning...LOL.!<BR>||||reg||1
